# bugs/ — RECORD OF EACH BUG FIX (interactive flow, skill bug-fix-flow)
#
# One folder per bug, written by the main session (agents only read it):
#
# bugs/
# └── <YYYYMMDD>-<slug>/
#     ├── report.md               expected, actual, steps, environment, error / log, violated scenario ID
#     ├── investigation.md        evidence log, call chain, ranked hypotheses, root cause,
#     │                           "Root cause: approved by user on <date>" (gate before any fix)
#     └── fix.md                  attempts (at most 3 failed), files changed, tests, verification,
#                                 same pattern elsewhere
#
# The folder is the whole record: to go on in a new chat, start from these three files only (no old chat log).
# Templates: .claude/skills/bug-fix-flow/templates/. Behavior no scenario covers is a spec gap, not a bug:
# it goes to the spec harness (/speckit-specify), not here.
